 "conventions": {
  "format": "JPEG, progressive. Colour maps 4:2:0 q82 (lawn q78); normal and packed maps 4:4:4 q85, except the noisy outdoor and carpet maps (exterior-stucco, lawn-grass, concrete-paving normal; carpet normal; exterior-stucco and lawn-grass orm at 256 px), which are 4:2:0 q70 to q75. Cards are WebP with alpha.",
  "packing": "orm.jpg = AO in red, roughness in green, metalness in blue. Assign the SAME texture object to aoMap, roughnessMap (and metalnessMap where channels.b is metalness). Set material.roughness = 1 and material.metalness = 1 only where channels.b is metalness, else 0.",
  "normal": "OpenGL convention, use as-is with normalMap (no Y flip).",
  "uv": "Set wrapS = wrapT = RepeatWrapping and repeat = surfaceSizeInMetres / sizeMeters so texel density is physically right.",
  "ao": "three.js r160 aoMap reads the first UV set (uv) by default; no uv2 needed.",
  "resolution": "Colour is always 1024. Fine-grained normal maps and most packed maps were reduced to 512 to meet the 6.5 MB budget; see px per map.",
  "tiers": "surfaces[slug].phone.skip lists maps the phone and low tiers do not download. maps[x].optional marks a map that nothing fetches by default. env.skyPhone replaces env.sky on phones. Phones also cap every texture at 512 px before upload (lab.html shrink())."
 },
